Z||000000||gt boy||10-22-2001||01:45 PM||||i know that this might sound like a silly question..but i am sure i read that a lot of people cursed armour all for their interior.<P>so i leave it up to my PFF friends to guide me to detailing sanity.<P><P>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."||||reg||5
Z||000001||watts||10-22-2001||02:03 PM||||Regular armour all sucks for most interior surfaces as it's very glossy, and will cause undesired reflections on your windows.<P>There are 'dull' versions of most products that are more suited for dash top's, etc.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||10-22-2001||02:22 PM||||not to mention that it is alcohol based and will cause cracking over time. There has been heated debate over this, but I know what I have seen, and seen what I know.<P>I go with formula 2001 ( bright green bottle ), silicon based and will not only clean but will replenish the moisture in the vinyl<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||10-22-2001||02:30 PM||||I once had a car that the previous owner had Armor-All'ed the sh!t out of the interior.<BR>One winter day the back seat backrest shattered when I leaned against it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>And if you leave your car closed up in the sun, it will evaporate and leave oily residue all over the inside of your windows. <BR>Armor All doesn't come within 50 feet of anything I own.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||13
Z||000004||stsmithgt||10-22-2001||04:14 PM||||Armor All bites the big one inside and out!  I use the 2001 like what WCF said.  I let years go by not using Armor All.  While my car was being washed at one of those fund raisers high school kids put on I saw them getting ready to squirt my tires down with the stuff.  I let them do it becuase I figured the product may have improved through the years, but in two days my tires had a brown tint and looked horrible.  And no, I didn't go down any dirt roads.  Needless to say I scrubbed them down and put on some 2001.  Problem solved.<P>Anything better than 2001??? <BR>mmmmmmm smell the synthetic leather imitation scent. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000005||rogergarrison||10-22-2001||06:26 PM||||20 years experience...in a word...NONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONONO<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>||||reg||1
