Z||000007||Indyrestoguy_JR||10-22-2001||06:48 PM||||I like Armour All's new Professional Stuff. It seems to work better than just the plain stuff. It seems to have more oil in it and does bring back faded plastic pieces, hince the oil. This is what I use in all cars I detail and has worked well for me. But, I do not drown anything in armour all because it has been known to crack and fade the pieces over time. I have not had anything crack or break on me. This is a paradox question... To each his own.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/imsa4.jpg">  <BR>85 IMSA<P>Do or Do Not, there is no Try.<p>[This message has been edited by Indyrestoguy_JR (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||10-22-2001||06:59 PM||||I've owned a few award winning big trucks.  I used to use Armor All.  The operative word is 'used to'.  Never again.  Cracked dashes and greased everything up.  Not only does it crack your dash, it also collects dust and dirt like you wouldn't beleive.  <B>Never</B> use Armor All!  All I use these days is some Windex and/or a damp rag.  ||||reg||1
